    description: "FOUND 2026-10-28 by WI-kalol's corpus A/B (dev 3c53837bb5 vs the WI-kalol branch, ~/hg_meas/kalol/docker-cli).\n\nIn a WHOLE-REPO survey of docker-cli, a receiver typed as a stdlib net type gets the PACKAGE in its module slot, not the type:\n  cli-plugins/socket/socket.go:68   conn, err := pl.l.Accept()   (pl.l is a *net.UnixListener field)  -> go:net:0-0:Accept   (on dev too)\n  cli-plugins/socket/socket.go:162  conn.Read(b), conn from net.DialUnix                              -> go:net:0-0:Read   (branch; external on dev)\nThe SAME file surveyed alone (module github.com/docker/cli, nothing else) emits go:net.UnixListener:0-0:Accept and go:net.UnixConn:0-0:Read. So something present in the full repository (vendor/, another package, a type registry collision -- not investigated) folds the qualified type to its package.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: io_boundary matches the bare `net` slot against the net.Conn rows by name and package-vs-type orthography (WI-monul's question), so the unix connection's read classifies as net_recv (the network medium) where the typed slot classifies as ipc_recv. Both mint untrusted_input; a network-zone claim reads a crossing that is local IPC.\n\nRepro: survey ~/ALL_REPOS/whole_bunch_of_repos/docker-cli and read the edges at socket.go:68 / :162; then survey that file alone in a fresh dir with a go.mod naming github.com/docker/cli."  # 1317
    fields: {}  # 1317
